From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 22:01:17 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] webOS: let the receiver ask the peer for a keyframe

A decoder that joins a video call mid-stream has nothing to decode until
the next IDR, and WhatsApp's encoders send IDRs on request rather than
on a short fixed cadence. The engine already sends PLI and FIR, but only
from its own ticker, and nothing outside the package can ask for one.

Add Call.RequestPeerKeyframe(). It posts to a one-slot channel, so
requests coalesce. The RTCP ticker goroutine serves each request with
the same PLI+FIR pair it already sends. The PLI/FIR send is factored
into one helper for both paths, so the FIR sequence number stays
consistent. A request made before the relay allocation is served right
after it.

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [webOS specific]
---
 engine_media.go | 37 ++++++++++++++++++++++++-------------
 livecall.go     | 22 ++++++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 46 insertions(+), 13 deletions(-)

diff --git a/engine_media.go b/engine_media.go
